stafeto is a POSIX system that is no Linux.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Copyright (C) 2026 Sergey Subbotin <ssubbotin@gmail.com>

Programs of stafeto are built for aarch64-linux-gnu, so the compiler defines
__linux__ (the headers of the C library test it) and the build adds
-D__stafeto__=1. detect_os.h makes that a POSIX system of its own,
DETECT_OS_STAFETO, with DETECT_OS_LINUX off, so the files that use the Linux
kernel's interfaces (epoll, eventfd, inotify, gettid, thread names, /proc)
take their other branches, and util/futex.h turns its futex path off for it by
decision (the sysroot has no <linux/futex.h> either). The direct tests of
__linux__ in the files the softpipe build compiles (u_queue.c, u_process.c) become DETECT_OS_LINUX, and
os_misc.c takes the sysconf branch for the page size and the memory.

diff --git a/src/util/detect_os.h b/src/util/detect_os.h
index 74037240..f16b4a5b 100644
--- a/src/util/detect_os.h
+++ b/src/util/detect_os.h
@@ -15,7 +15,19 @@
 #ifndef DETECT_OS_H
 #define DETECT_OS_H
 
-#if defined(__linux__)
+/*
+ * stafeto programs are built for aarch64-linux-gnu, so the compiler defines
+ * __linux__ (the headers of its C library test it), and the build adds
+ * -D__stafeto__=1. The system is a POSIX one that is no Linux: nothing of the
+ * Linux kernel's interfaces (epoll, eventfd, inotify, gettid, thread names)
+ * is there, and the futex path of util/futex.h is off by decision (futex.h
+ * tests DETECT_OS_STAFETO), so Mesa waits on the C library's mutexes and
+ * condition variables.
+ */
+#if defined(__stafeto__)
+#define DETECT_OS_STAFETO 1
+#define DETECT_OS_POSIX 1
+#elif defined(__linux__)
 #define DETECT_OS_LINUX 1
 #define DETECT_OS_POSIX 1
 #endif
